Hi Backend Team,

We encountered a bug on the admin panel: **Admins are unable to revoke old admin-granted subscriptions.** The API throws the error: *"Cannot revoke store-purchased subscriptions..."*

### 🐛 The Root Cause
When the new `source` field was added to the [Subscription](file:///c:/MAFSFrontend/mafs_frontend/src/modules/users/components/Tabs/subscription.Tab.jsx#31-276) schema, the `default` was set to `"STORE"`. Because of this, **all old subscriptions** (which were granted manually by admins via `platform: "admin_granted"`) now evaluate as `source: "STORE"`. 

The `/revoke` endpoint relies on the `source` field to restrict action. Since the old admin grants now look like store purchases, the backend incorrectly blocks the revoke action.

---

### 🛠️ Required Fixes

Please apply these two changes to fully resolve the issue without any future bugs:

#### 1. Update the Controller Logic (Immediate Fix)
In **`modules/subscription/controllers/admin.controller.js`** inside the [revokeSubscription](file:///c:/MAFSFrontend/mafs_frontend/src/modules/subsciptions/services/subscription.services.js#95-99) function, update the restriction condition to properly ignore old `"admin_granted"` platforms.

**Change this:**
```javascript
        // Restrict revoking store-purchased subscriptions
        if (activeSubscription.source === "STORE") {
            return res.status(400).json({
                success: false,
                message: "Cannot revoke store-purchased subscriptions. User must request refund through Apple/Google."
            });
        }
```

**To this:**
```javascript
        // Restrict revoking store-purchased subscriptions (fallback check for old records)
        const isStorePurchase = activeSubscription.source === "STORE" && activeSubscription.platform !== "admin_granted";
        
        if (isStorePurchase) {
            return res.status(400).json({
                success: false,
                message: "Cannot revoke store-purchased subscriptions. User must request refund through Apple/Google."
            });
        }
```

<br/>

#### 2. Run a One-Time Database Migration (Data Cleanup)
To ensure our analytics and dashboard metrics are 100% accurate, we need to fix the old database records. Please run this script in the MongoDB shell or via a temporary route:

```javascript
// Step 1: Fix old manual admin grants (that incorrectly defaulted to STORE)
await mongoose.model("Subscription").updateMany(
    { 
        platform: "admin_granted", 
        source: "STORE",
        grantReason: { $not: /milestone/i } 
    },
    { $set: { source: "ADMIN" } }
);

// Step 2: Fix old Giveaway/Milestone grants (if any)
await mongoose.model("Subscription").updateMany(
    { 
        platform: "admin_granted", 
        source: "STORE",
        grantReason: /milestone/i 
    },
    { $set: { source: "GIVEAWAY" } }
);
```

Let me know once this is deployed so I can test it on the frontend!
